1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,609
Communication uses MQTT only.

2
00:00:02,609 --> 00:00:12,815
There are separate topics for telemetry, metadata, status, twin state, twin alarms, load commands, fault injection, and what-if requests and responses.

3
00:00:12,815 --> 00:00:15,813
Telemetry and twin outputs use QoS one.

4
00:00:15,813 --> 00:00:22,766
Meta and status are retained, so a dashboard that connects late immediately knows the units and the asset state.

5
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:29,417
Status also configures a last will: if the simulator dies, the broker publishes offline, retained.

6
00:00:29,417 --> 00:00:35,533
The ingestor uses a persistent session, so a normal disconnect does not drop QoS one messages.

7
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:37,621
Commands are logged to SQLite.

8
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,320
Field names carry units.

9
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:43,919
In the demo you will see actual topic traffic and the resulting dashboard updates.

